<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:57:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How AI visionary Jensen Huang was undone by his own bad decisions</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq5y13819gpjo#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:57:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:43:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq5y13819gpjo--376d5a6f39d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq5y13819gpjo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Zoe Kleinman explains how the man who built Nvidia from the ground up lost everything in a matter of days.</summary></entry><entry><title>The rise and fall of Jensen Huang - how the tech superstar became mired in scandal</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmze750zg0jeo#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:02:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmze750zg0jeo--00916c7a76a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmze750zg0jeo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Within days, Huang's status as a seemingly untouchable figure leading the global tech race has crumbled.</summary></entry><entry><title>What we know as Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns over affair allegations</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgel338xql3o#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:26:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgel338xql3o--e869dd4c2eff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgel338xql3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The billionaire tech executive has left the company following reports of a second extramarital affair.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is Nvidia's interim CEO Colette Kress - and who could take over permanently?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqgm37dv20e8o#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:10:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqgm37dv20e8o--a603fb20f5ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqgm37dv20e8o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Chief financial officer Colette Kress in in charge of Nvidia for now, but several others are in the frame as potential successors.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lego marketplace BrickLink offline after 'unusual activity' detected</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rmgw8zynr4o#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T22:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rmgw8zynr4o--76c32aad363e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rmgw8zynr4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Known as the eBay of Lego, it has been down for three days and is yet to disclose what caused the shutdown.</summary></entry><entry><title>New Indian mega library rocked by scandal over 'AI-generated books'</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c54gne3plvrxo#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:33:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c54gne3plvrxo--f2638f7d630e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c54gne3plvrxo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Tamil Nadu government has ordered an internal audit of library collections across the state.</summary></entry><entry><title>Robot vessels take on the dangerous work of mine hunting</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj5yn24llxd6o#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T00:19:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj5yn24llxd6o--b2f23fe60f3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj5yn24llxd6o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The conflict in the Gulf is an opportunity for the US to test its autonomous mine-hunting systems.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia hires major US law firm to investigate alleged Chinese spy affair</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck1wvwwl3x0go#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T22:52:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck1wvwwl3x0go--9435eb245211.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck1wvwwl3x0go?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The appointment was made after it emerged Jensen Huang had an affair with a woman believed to be a spy for China.</summary></entry><entry><title>Claude chatbot maker set for $1.3tn stock market debut despite 'catastrophic' AI warning</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdgd723x2zo#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:56:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdgd723x2zo--c67f8109386f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdgd723x2zo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The AI company behind the Claude chatbot will offer its shares at between $70 and $78, which is lower than what was expected.</summary></entry><entry><title>Faisal Islam: What the boss of US tech giant Nvidia told me about China and national security</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64g1gzy2vdzo#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T09:23:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64g1gzy2vdzo--9d5d87a4a477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64g1gzy2vdzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Huang, who is now being investigated over an affair with an alleged Chinese spy, is far more important to the future of the world order than other tech bosses.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says FBI investigating Nvidia boss's affair with alleged Chinese spy</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqg7x7dpvym8o#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:23:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqg7x7dpvym8o--4a9293f6fb18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqg7x7dpvym8o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The US president said he spoke with Jensen Huang on Monday and asked him about the affair with the alleged spy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Australia considers criminal penalties for rogue AI in wake of OpenAI hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmp3g37l566po#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T05:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmp3g37l566po--d4036d1f11fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmp3g37l566po?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI safety regulator will also be created after a rogue OpenAI agent hacked government websites.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zoe Kleinman: Nvidia CEO's affair will cause ripples across US and beyond</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj3vqv3nee72o#0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:52:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj3vqv3nee72o--a4177bf4c675.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj3vqv3nee72o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang is being investigated by his own company over an extramarital affair with a woman alleged to be a Chinese spy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv#2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv--9798c5d5f4ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">We investigate internet-connected device flaws worldwide, plus US election tech fallout.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt#2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt--974b9860edd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">When copyright strikes silence reporters, rail safety &amp; the Lord of the Rings live show.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jys#2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jys--8346efbd8e2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jys?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">We hear from Ondřej Surý, the programmer whose PHP patches helped avert a cyber crisis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyl#2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyl--b40d7991507a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyl?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The next generation of chip is thinner and flexible when compared to traditional silicon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032yng#3</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T01:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032yng--a0e77a89b85a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032yng?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Shiona McCallum visits Cairngorms National Park to see tech monitor wildfire damage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032n6v#3</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T01:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032n6v--2d0c1972c36b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032n6v?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Alasdair Keane heads to the Pokémon World Championships in San Francisco.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032d9k#3</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T01:00:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032d9k--c78bd9d9cf81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032d9k?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Ammie Sekhon explores tech used to identify and remove counterfeit products online.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032301#3</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T01:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032301--6cdb0ccc5e11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032301?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Adrienne Murray follows NASA scientists in Iceland researching a rare total solar eclipse.</summary></entry></feed>
